{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md at exact 7bc60cf6b96f5408340c34042d2d60f409eda94d on request/authority-publication, under promise git:sha1…34c6367 on request git:sha1…bdda9ac\n\nAuthority, effects and publication, revision 16 at 7bc60cf6b96f5408340c34042d2d60f409eda94d, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 60c940f3 on 8dfda899: the main note, its corrections and the dated facts (the facts file is unchanged). Finding 1, stop admission at the item limit: room is reserved inside the one control type. An ordinary control is admitted only while fewer than 62 of the six non-stop kinds are queued, else refused controls-full. At most one pause and one cancel are queued at once; a second of the same kind is refused stop-pending or answered as a repeat. A task reserves entries for one cancel from its establishment and for one pause from the apply of a start or resume. So an authorized stop is at most the 64th item and is always admitted, or is a repeat of a live one, or the task is already cancelling or ended. Voided controls stay as records. Finding 2, a replacement restore after a failed recovery: a restore refused with one of the recovery design's five reasons opens a failure item, undecided. While it is undecided every restore's intend is refused recovery-undecided, under that registration or a new one. A new act, decide-recovery, signed by a device key of the controller or an admin under task.control, which the agent role does not hold, names the failure exactly and chooses repair or abandon. Repair admits one replacement; a second failure needs a new decision. Abandon fences the registration and the next chain starts from the hold's fork. A first restore, a restore after host loss and a new instance after an unknown outcome need no decision. Precedence: a pause's outcome voids every queued start and resume. Narrowed, and listed in the corrections file: ordinary queued controls 64 to 62; a second same-kind stop refused; start and resume refused while a stop is queued. The author's adversarial re-read found and closed two holes in its own draft, recorded in the corrections file. Points a reviewer may question, stated in the note: a restore already in flight that is then confirmed lapses the failure with no decision; the failure reason is the runtime's report; the standing room for a stop is declared by this note and its form is owed under P11. Reading limits: revision 15 was not read again in full; the contract and the recovery design were read in the cited sections. Design only: nothing was run.","body":{"commit":"7bc60cf6b96f5408340c34042d2d60f409eda94d","path":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md"}}